Request: Schedule payment for the Umbrella Office Furniture bill.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Schedule payment for the Umbrella Office Furniture bill.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants the outstanding invoice from vendor 'Umbrella Office Furniture' to be paid on its due date through the ERP: the bill must exist
in the ERP (recording it first if it is not yet there), a payment must be scheduled for the due date (with Finance Manager approval first if the amount is ≥ INR
50,000), and the AP lead must be notified with the bill ID, amount and payment date.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A confirmation to the user containing the vendor name, invoice number, amount (INR incl. GST), ERP bill ID, scheduled payment date and the 
approval/fraud-report status — backed by the ERP bill/payment record and the confirmation email sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Finance controls policy: payments ≥ INR 50,000 require Finance Manager (arjun.mehta@kestrel.in) approval BEFORE the payment is scheduled; the ERP will route
this for approval.
  - Vendor bank details are never changed and never taken from an email; payment goes to the bank account already on file.
  - Vendor master records can only be approved by the Finance Manager; AP/automated operators must not create or approve vendors.
  - No emails may be sent to any address outside @kestrel.in without prior human approval (the confirmation to Priya is internal, so it is allowed).
  - The invoice sender's email domain must exactly match the vendor's registered email_domain in the ERP; on mismatch, do not process — report suspected fraud 
to priya.nair@kestrel.in and stop.
  - Check for duplicates before recording: if a bill with the same invoice number for that vendor already exists in the ERP, do not record it again — report the
existing bill ID and status.
  - Never use admin/test endpoints of any system; all ERP writes (record bill, schedule payment) are GUI-only and require login.
  - Dates entered in the ERP must be in YYYY-MM-DD format.
  - Do not email the vendor any confirmation (not asked, and not permitted without approval).
  - Scope discipline: because the request is only to schedule payment, only read the invoice email if the bill is NOT already in the ERP.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. The ERP vendor master contains exactly one vendor matching 'Umbrella Office Furniture' and its record (including bank details and email_domain) is 
identical to how it was found — no vendor was created, edited or approved by the operator.
  C2. Exactly one ERP bill exists for the Umbrella Office Furniture invoice — either it already existed and was reported as-is, or it was recorded once now — 
with the invoice number, invoice date, due date and total amount (INR incl. GST) matching the source invoice; no duplicate bill was created.
  C3. Either a payment is scheduled in the ERP on the bill's due date, OR — for amounts ≥ INR 50,000 — the payment was scheduled only after Finance Manager 
approval was granted; if approval was refused or still pending, no payment is scheduled and this is reported instead of being worked around.
  C4. If and only if the invoice sender domain failed to match the vendor master, no bill was recorded and no payment was scheduled for it, and a 
suspected-fraud report was sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in.
  C5. Exactly one confirmation email was sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in containing vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID and payment date; no email was sent to
any non-@kestrel.in address.
  C6. No unintended or policy-violating changes were made: no vendor bank-detail change, no vendor creation/approval, no external email, no admin/test endpoint 
usage, and no ERP record touched other than the single bill/payment needed for this invoice.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - 'Umbrella Office Furniture' is a vendor already registered in the ERP vendor master.
  - The request concerns a single invoice; if multiple invoices exist, the single unpaid one is intended.
  - Today is 2026-10-10; the payment should be scheduled for the invoice due date (if the due date is already past, schedule for the due date as recorded and 
flag it rather than silently changing it).
  - Because the request is specifically to schedule payment, the invoice email only needs to be read if the bill is not yet in the ERP.
  - The confirmation to Priya Nair is internal (@kestrel.in) and therefore does not require external-email approval.
PLAN:
  S1: Look up the vendor 'Umbrella Office Furniture' in the ERP vendor master (read-only API first). (done when: vendor_id, vendor name and registered 
email_domain are known; ambiguity (zero or multiple matches) is identified.)
  S2: Look up existing bills for that vendor in the ERP to determine whether the invoice is already recorded (read-only API). (done when: Either one matching 
bill is found (bill_id, invoice number, amount incl. GST, due date, status known) or it is confirmed no bill exists for this invoice.)
  S3: If no bill exists, locate the email in the AP mailbox whose attachment is the Umbrella Office Furniture invoice (follow-ups/reminders without attachments 
are skipped) and verify the sender domain exactly matches the vendor master's email_domain. (done when: Invoice PDF/image is located and the sender domain check
passes, or — on mismatch — processing stops.)
  S4: If the sender-domain check fails, report suspected fraud to priya.nair@kestrel.in and stop without recording or paying anything. (done when: Fraud report 
email is in the Sent folder and no ERP bill/payment exists for this invoice.)
  S5: If no bill exists and verification passed, record the bill once in the ERP via the GUI with vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date (YYYY-MM-DD) 
and total incl. GST, after a duplicate check. (done when: ERP shows exactly one new bill for this invoice with correct fields; no duplicate exists.)
  S6: Schedule payment for the bill's due date in the ERP via the GUI (approval-gated action: ≥ INR 50,000 routes to the Finance Manager for approval before 
scheduling). (done when: ERP bill shows a payment scheduled on the due date, or approval is pending/refused and the outcome is reported without a schedule.)
  S7: Email the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) the confirmation with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID and payment date. (done when: Confirmation email 
is present in the Sent folder addressed only to priya.nair@kestrel.in.)
